{"parentUuid":"18da0f8e-0d8d-4c66-b4f7-f72a0cf17fe3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBwB59UpdJZGdHrtJwmw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Committing #348:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":404009,"output_tokens":1016,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":404009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef9df6e9-2a38-4d61-a8c4-b7e2cbbe9e63","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBwB4mRVif8KTvbgFwND","requestRef":"47cdce78-39c1-4be5-870e-3384cb813044","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5da2f847-6793-467a-96b6-fcb93473606e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T16:46:15.551Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-runnable-remedies","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"5da2f847-6793-467a-96b6-fcb93473606e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBwB59UpdJZGdHrtJwmw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YUGrmsL6HXqK6qh8GRgRki","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into the runnable-remedies branch\n\nTwo conflicts, resolved in opposite directions because they are opposite cases.\n\npublish.go  -> took MAIN. This branch still carried the ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED\n            opt-in gate; main retired it in c6c3eed3 (\"Retire\n            ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED; canonicalize the kill switch as\n            ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\", COR-2111/COR-2116). Keeping this branch's\n            side would have re-introduced a variable the product deliberately\n            removed. Checked the history before deciding, not the diff.\n\nsemantic.go -> took BOTH. Main gates the live provider probe behind `audit`;\n            this branch makes the remedy runnable. The merge keeps main's\n            gating and renders its remedy through brainInvocation.\n\nThen this PR's own guard did its job. TestNoHardcodedBrainSpellingInPrintedRemedies\nfailed on EIGHT sites that main added after this branch was cut:\n\n  session_privacy_verify.go  1  printed remedy  -> brainInvocation\n  hosted_target.go           4  printed remedies -> brainInvocation\n  hosted_status.go           2  printed remedies -> brainInvocation\n  disconnect_cmd.go          1  printed banner   -> brainInvocation\n\nand two cobra Long help strings (publish.go, disconnect_cmd.go) that are built\nat command-construction time, before any lookup exists. Those go in\ndeliberatelyHardcoded under the SAME reason the existing add.go entry gives --\na category, not a per-line excuse.\n\nTwo tests main brought in pinned the literal \"entire brain connect\":\nhosted_status_test.go and publish_test.go. They now assert through\nbrainInvocation, which is the pattern the rest of this branch's tests already\nuse (dash_test, facts_integrity_test, mcp_missing_brain_note_test). That is the\npoint of the PR: the spelling is the reader's, not a constant.\n\nVerified by weakening: dropping the rendered remedy from hosted_status.go makes\nTestStatusHostedDisconnectedByOptOut fail; restored, green -- so the rewritten\nassertions are not vacuous.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green (0 failing of the whole package), every other\npackage green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/runnable-remedies 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push 348"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":404009,"output_tokens":1016,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":404009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YUGrmsL6HXqK6qh8GRgRki":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-runnable-remedies && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into the runnable-remedies branch\n\nTwo conflicts, resolved in opposite directions because they are opposite cases.\n\npublish.go  -> took MAIN. This branch still carried the ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED\n            opt-in gate; main retired it in c6c3eed3 (\"Retire\n            ENTIRE_BRAIN_ALLOW_HOSTED; canonicalize the kill switch as\n            ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\", COR-2111/COR-2116). Keeping this branch's\n            side would have re-introduced a variable the product deliberately\n            removed. Checked the history before deciding, not the diff.\n\nsemantic.go -> took BOTH. Main gates the live provider probe behind `audit`;\n            this branch makes the remedy runnable. The merge keeps main's\n            gating and renders its remedy through brainInvocation.\n\nThen this PR's own guard did its job. TestNoHardcodedBrainSpellingInPrintedRemedies\nfailed on EIGHT sites that main added after this branch was cut:\n\n  session_privacy_verify.go  1  printed remedy  -> brainInvocation\n  hosted_target.go           4  printed remedies -> brainInvocation\n  hosted_status.go           2  printed remedies -> brainInvocation\n  disconnect_cmd.go          1  printed banner   -> brainInvocation\n\nand two cobra Long help strings (publish.go, disconnect_cmd.go) that are built\nat command-construction time, before any lookup exists. Those go in\ndeliberatelyHardcoded under the SAME reason the existing add.go entry gives --\na category, not a per-line excuse.\n\nTwo tests main brought in pinned the literal \"entire brain connect\":\nhosted_status_test.go and publish_test.go. They now assert through\nbrainInvocation, which is the pattern the rest of this branch's tests already\nuse (dash_test, facts_integrity_test, mcp_missing_brain_note_test). That is the\npoint of the PR: the spelling is the reader's, not a constant.\n\nVerified by weakening: dropping the rendered remedy from hosted_status.go makes\nTestStatusHostedDisconnectedByOptOut fail; restored, green -- so the rewritten\nassertions are not vacuous.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green (0 failing of the whole package), every other\npackage green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/runnable-remedies 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push